## 5. Revised ML Architecture for Production

### Replace DINOv2 with ConvAE

| Component | Old Plan (DINOv2) | New Plan (ConvAE) |
|---|---|---|
| Vision model | DINOv2-small (400MB) + Head | **Custom ConvAE (~8MB ONNX)** |
| Training data | 500+ normal images | **10,000–26,000 normal images** |
| Inference time CPU | 5–15 sec | **0.1–0.5 sec** |
| Deployment | GPU required | **Any CPU server** |
| Heatmap method | Grad-CAM (complex) | **Pixel-diff reconstruction map** |

### Revised Model Stack

```
KEEP:    BioBERT NER (fine-tuned) → export to ONNX for fast CPU
KEEP:    MiniLM-L6 (RAG embeddings) → fast, CPU-native
KEEP:    BioGPT (report + chat) → runs on CPU, acceptable speed
KEEP:    Whisper-Tiny → CPU, works fine
REPLACE: DINOv2 + Head → Custom ConvAE (ONNX-exported)
DROP:    BiomedVLP (900MB, optional) → use keyword fallback in production
```

### Final Production Memory Footprint

| Model | Format | RAM |
|---|---|---|
| ConvAE | ONNX | ~50MB |
| BioBERT NER | ONNX | ~200MB |
| MiniLM | native | ~100MB |
| BioGPT | PyTorch | ~700MB |
| Whisper-tiny | native | ~150MB |
| **Total** | | **~1.2GB RAM** |

This runs on a **2GB RAM server** — no GPU needed.

---

## 6. Recommended Build Order

```
Step 1: Write ConvAE architecture + training script
        → Input: NIH ChestX-ray14 "No Finding" images
        → Output: chest_convae.onnx (8MB)

Step 2: Fine-tune BioBERT NER + export to ONNX
        → Input: NCBI Disease Corpus
        → Output: biobert_ner.onnx (440MB → 220MB quantized)

Step 3: Download & test pretrained models (no training)
        → BioGPT, MiniLM, Whisper

Step 4: Fetch PubMed abstracts → populate ChromaDB

Step 5: Wire everything into AnalysisPipeline using ONNX Runtime
```

> **Say "build the ConvAE training script" and I'll write the full training code with dataset download, training loop, ONNX export, and stats calibration.**
